messages:
Anna L: quick check — about to land a TF change that splits the ExternalSecret serviceAccount into two: `extsecrets-controller-sa` (controller, read) and `rotation-agent-sa` (rotation jobs, write). goal is smaller blast radius for rotation jobs. plan looks okay locally but want an RBAC/annotation sanity check. @Mike R can you take a quick look?

Mike R: yep — pinged. quick q: are the rotation cronjobs running in the same namespace as the ExternalSecrets (vault-sync)? if yes we need a RoleBinding for `rotation-agent-sa` in that ns with `secrets:create` and `secrets:update`. also double-check projected token settings for the jobs.

Anna L: yes cronjobs live in `vault-sync`. here's the relevant TF diff I'm about to apply (abridged):

```hcl
resource "kubernetes_service_account" "rotation_agent" {
  metadata {
    name = "rotation-agent"
    namespace = "vault-sync"
    annotations = {
      "externalsecret.redwood.io/rotation-svc" = "rotation-agent"
    }
  }
}

resource "kubernetes_role_binding" "rotation_agent_bind" {
  metadata { name = "rotation-agent-bind" namespace = "vault-sync" }
  role_ref { kind = "Role" name = "rotation-job-role" }
  subject { kind = "ServiceAccount" name = kubernetes_service_account.rotation_agent.metadata[0].name namespace = "vault-sync" }
}
```

devops-bot: Deploy-bot: terraform plan finished in CI — no surprises. Plan URL: https://ci.redwood.internal/plan/38291 (expires in 24h) :white_check_mark:

Jules: LGTM overall. couple notes: add annotation `externalsecret.redwood.io/rotation-svc: rotation-agent` (you already have it) and set ExternalSecret TTL to a sane value, e.g. `externalSecrets.kubernetes.io/ttl: "1h"`. also validate with `kubectl auth can-i create secrets --as=system:serviceaccount:vault-sync:rotation-agent` before applying.

Anna L: ok adding TTL annotation. running the can-i check now and will attach output to the PR. one more question: do we need to alter anything for projected service account tokens? the cronjobs mount tokens with audiences. @DevEx are there gating scripts we should run?

DevEx: there's a preflight helper at `infra/tools/sa-check.sh` — run `./infra/tools/sa-check.sh rotation-agent vault-sync` (it validates SA annotations, token projection, and RBAC binds). also remember to add a short note in `infra/CHANGELOG.md` mentioning the split so oncall knows why rotation jobs use a different SA.

Mike R: add to that — ensure ExternalSecret objects explicitly set `serviceAccountName: rotation-agent` in the spec (if not, controller will act with controller SA and rotation jobs will still fail). also update vault path template to use the new rotation namespace path: `secret/data/rotations/{{namespace}}/{{name}}` so we don't collide with other secrets.

Anna L: thanks all — I'll push an updated commit with the annotation + TTL + rolebinding and run the `sa-check.sh` and `kubectl auth can-i` checks. marking PR ready for review after CI runs. :pray:
